{"additionalPlain":"\"We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, age, disability, genetic information or any other category protected by law.\n \nBy applying for this position, you acknowledge that your personal information will be processed as per the Lyra Health Workforce Privacy Notice. Through this application, to the extent permitted by law, we will collect personal information from you including, but not limited to, your name, email address, gender identity, employment information, and phone number for the purposes of recruiting and assessing suitability, aptitude, skills, qualifications, and interests for employment with Lyra.  We may also collect information about your race, ethnicity, and sexual orientation, which is considered sensitive personal information under the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA) and special category data under the UK and EU GDPR.  Providing this information is optional and completely voluntary, and if you provide it you consent to Lyra processing it for the purposes as described at the point of collection, for example for diversity and inclusion initiatives.  If you are a California resident and would like to limit how we use this information, please use the Limit the Use of My Sensitive Personal Information form.  This information will only be retained for as long as needed to fulfill the purposes for which it was collected, as described above. Please note that Lyra does not “sell” or “share” personal information as defined by the CPRA. Outside of the United States, for example in the EU, Switzerland and the UK, you may have the right to request access to, or a copy of, your personal information, including in a portable format; request that we delete your information from our systems; object to or restrict processing of your information; or correct inaccurate or outdated personal information in our systems. These rights may be subject to legal limitations. To exercise your data privacy rights outside of the United States, please contact globaldpo@lyrahealth.com. For more information about how we use and retain your information, please see our Workforce Privacy Notice.\"\n","additional":"<div><span style=\"font-size: small;\">\"</span><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, age, disability,&nbsp;genetic information or any other category protected by law.</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">By applying for this position,&nbsp;you acknowledge that&nbsp;your&nbsp;personal information&nbsp;will be processed as per&nbsp;the&nbsp;Lyra Health&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.lyrahealth.com/workforce-privacy-notice/\" style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">Workforce Privacy Notice</a><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">. Through this application, to the extent permitted by law,&nbsp;we will collect personal information from you including, but not limited to,&nbsp;your name, email address, gender identity, employment information, and phone number for the purposes of recruiting and assessing suitability, aptitude, skills, qualifications, and interests for employment with Lyra.&nbsp;&nbsp;We may also collect information about your race, ethnicity, and sexual orientation, which is considered sensitive personal information under the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA)&nbsp;and special category data under the UK and EU GDPR.&nbsp; Providing this information is optional and completely voluntary,&nbsp;and if you provide it you consent to Lyra processing it for the purposes as described at the point of collection, for example for diversity and inclusion initiatives.&nbsp; If you are a California resident and would like to limit how we use this information, please use the Limit the Use of My Sensitive Personal Information&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://privacy-central.securiti.ai/#/dsr/be61bec1-10a5-47ac-94ab-3055974aefb1\" style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">form</a><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">.&nbsp; This information will only be retained for as long as needed to fulfill the purposes for which it was collected, as described above. Please note that Lyra does not “sell” or “share” personal information as defined by the CPRA.&nbsp;Outside of the United States, for example in the EU, Switzerland and the UK, you may have the right to request access to, or a copy of, your personal information, including in a portable format; request that we delete your information from our systems; object to or restrict processing of your information; or correct inaccurate or outdated personal information in our systems. These rights may be subject to legal limitations.&nbsp;To exercise your data privacy rights outside of the United States, please contact&nbsp;</span><a href=\"mailto:globaldpo@lyrahealth.com\" style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">globaldpo@lyrahealth.com</a><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">.</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">&nbsp;For more information about how we use and retain your information, please see our&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.lyrahealth.com/workforce-privacy-notice/\" style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">Workforce Privacy Notice</a><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">.\"</span></div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full-time","department":"Provider Network Ops","location":"United States","team":"Provider Network Operations","allLocations":["United States"]},"createdAt":1787252730515,"descriptionPlain":"About Lyra Health\nLyra Health is a leading provider of evidence-based mental health care, serving more than 20 million people globally in partnership with employers and more than 100 million through health plan and partner relationships. The company has delivered more than 15 million sessions of mental health care, published more than 35 peer-reviewed studies, and delivered unmatched outcomes in terms of access, clinical effectiveness, and cost efficiency. Extensive peer-reviewed research confirms Lyra’s transformative care model helps people recover twice as fast and results in a 26% annual reduction in overall healthcare claims costs. Lyra is transforming access to life-changing mental health care through Lyra Empower, the only fully integrated, AI-powered platform combining the highest-quality care and technology solutions. \n\n\nAbout The Role\nWe are seeking an experienced Director of Operations – Provider Performance to establish and execute a holistic provider performance strategy across all of Lyra’s clinical service lines. In this role, you will lead a high-impact team operating at the intersection of clinical strategy, data analytics, and operational execution. Your mandate is to optimize provider performance which will further drive clinical quality, client access to care, and business results.\nAs a strategic player-coach, you will partner closely with Service Line leaders, Clinical Operations, and Data Analytics to build scalable data infrastructure, operational tools, and executive reporting. You will translate complex performance insights into actionable dashboards and operational systems that drive data visibility for providers, managers and executive leadership.\n","description":"<div><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><strong>About Lyra Health</strong></span></div>\n<div>Lyra Health is a leading provider of evidence-based mental health care, serving more than 20 million people globally in partnership with employers and more than 100 million through health plan and partner relationships. The company has delivered more than 15 million sessions of mental health care, published more than 35 peer-reviewed studies, and delivered unmatched outcomes in terms of access, clinical effectiveness, and cost efficiency. Extensive peer-reviewed research confirms Lyra’s transformative care model helps people recover twice as fast and results in a 26% annual reduction in overall healthcare claims costs. Lyra is transforming access to life-changing mental health care through Lyra Empower, the only fully integrated, AI-powered platform combining the highest-quality care and technology solutions. </div><div><br></div><div>\n<p><strong>About The Role</strong></p>\n<p>We are seeking an experienced <strong>Director of Operations – Provider Performance</strong> to establish and execute a holistic provider performance strategy across all of Lyra’s clinical service lines. In this role, you will lead a high-impact team operating at the intersection of clinical strategy, data analytics, and operational execution. Your mandate is to optimize provider performance which will further drive clinical quality, client access to care, and business results.</p>\n<p>As a strategic player-coach, you will partner closely with Service Line leaders, Clinical Operations, and Data Analytics to build scalable data infrastructure, operational tools, and executive reporting. You will translate complex performance insights into actionable dashboards and operational systems that drive data visibility for providers, managers and executive leadership.</p>\n</div>","id":"1fc1bb17-b865-4fb3-ac0a-7053569d2d59","lists":[{"text":"What You’ll Do:","content":"<div>\n\n<li>\n<p><strong>Strategic Vision &amp; Roadmap Ownership:</strong> Define and execute a holistic provider performance vision, establishing standardized, scalable frameworks across all clinical service lines</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Team Leadership &amp; Scale:</strong> Lead, mentor, and build a high-performing operations team. Set high-impact priorities and support professional development for direct reports.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Data Vision &amp; Analytics Governance:</strong> Partner directly with the Data Analytics team to build a unified data vision. Establish centralized systems to measure, track, and predict provider availability, capacity, and performance across diverse employment models</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Systems &amp; Tooling Execution:</strong> Oversee the development of operational tools, workflows, and cross-program dashboards that empower clinical managers to drive day-to-day performance and provide executive leadership with real-time visibility&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Strategic Cross-Functional Leadership:</strong> Serve as a core operational partner to senior leadership on strategic growth initiatives, with an immediate focus on optimizing provider availability, network utilization, and productivity across our Adult Outpatient Service Line</p>\n</li>\n\n</div>"},{"text":"Requirements:","content":"<div>\n\n<li>\n<p><strong>Core Requirement — Provider Performance Experience</strong>: 5+ years of direct, hands-on experience designing, scaling, or managing provider performance operations, clinical productivity frameworks, or provider network operations within a healthcare organization, health tech company, or large provider network<strong>.</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>15+ years</strong> of experience in business operations, management consulting, healthcare operations, or high-growth health tech; experience scaling complex operations preferred.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>8+ years</strong> of direct people management experience, with a track record of scaling high-performing teams and building strong team cultures.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Domain Knowledge of Provider Metrics: </strong>Deep understanding of clinical network operations and core provider metrics (e.g., panel management, utilization rates, clinical outcome tracking)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Data &amp; Analytics Expertise:</strong> Proven ability to scope analytical frameworks, synthesize complex data sets, and partner effectively with analytics teams to translate raw data into operational tools and dashboards.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Executive Influence:</strong> Demonstrated experience building strategic roadmaps and aligning executive leadership, clinical leaders, and cross-functional teams around shared outcomes.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Execution &amp; Change Management:</strong> A self-starter who thrives in ambiguous environments, with a proven ability to turn complex, disparate processes into standardized, scalable systems.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Mission Alignment:</strong> Passionate about expanding access to high-quality, evidence-based mental health care.</p>\n</li>\n\n</div>"}],"salaryRange":{"min":134000,"max":184000,"currency":"USD","interval":"per-year-salary"},"salaryDescription":"<div><span data-sheets-root=\"1\">As a full-time Director, Operations - Provider Performance, you will be employed by Lyra Health, Inc. The anticipated annual base salary range for this full-time position is $134,000 - $184,000. The base range is determined by role and level, and placement within the range will depend on a number of job-related factors, including but not limited to your skills, qualifications, experience and location. This role may also be eligible for discretionary bonuses.&nbsp;<br><br>Annual salary is only one part of an employee’s total compensation package at Lyra. We also offer generous benefits that include: <br><br>Comprehensive healthcare coverage (including medical, dental, vision, FSA/HSA, life and disability insurances)<br>Lyra for Lyrians; coaching and therapy services<br>Equity in the company through discretionary restricted stock units<br>Competitive time off with pay policies including vacation, sick days, and company holidays<br>Paid parental leave <br>401K with up to 3% matching<br>Monthly tech allowance<br>We like to spread joy throughout the year with well-being perks and activities, surprise swag, regular community celebration…and more! <br><br>We can’t wait to meet you.</span></div>","salaryDescriptionPlain":"As a full-time Director, Operations - Provider Performance, you will be employed by Lyra Health, Inc. The anticipated annual base salary range for this full-time position is $134,000 - $184,000. The base range is determined by role and level, and placement within the range will depend on a number of job-related factors, including but not limited to your skills, qualifications, experience and location. This role may also be eligible for discretionary bonuses. \n\nAnnual salary is only one part of an employee’s total compensation package at Lyra. We also offer generous benefits that include: \n\nComprehensive healthcare coverage (including medical, dental, vision, FSA/HSA, life and disability insurances)\nLyra for Lyrians; coaching and therapy services\nEquity in the company through discretionary restricted stock units\nCompetitive time off with pay policies including vacation, sick days, and company holidays\nPaid parental leave \n401K with up to 3% matching\nMonthly tech allowance\nWe like to spread joy throughout the year with well-being perks and activities, surprise swag, regular community celebration…and more! \n\nWe can’t wait to meet you.\n","text":"Director, Operations - Provider Performance","country":"US","workplaceType":"remote","opening":"<div><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><strong>About Lyra Health</strong></span></div>\n<div>Lyra Health is a leading provider of evidence-based mental health care, serving more than 20 million people globally in partnership with employers and more than 100 million through health plan and partner relationships. The company has delivered more than 15 million sessions of mental health care, published more than 35 peer-reviewed studies, and delivered unmatched outcomes in terms of access, clinical effectiveness, and cost efficiency. Extensive peer-reviewed research confirms Lyra&rsquo;s transformative care model helps people recover twice as fast and results in a 26% annual reduction in overall healthcare claims costs. Lyra is transforming access to life-changing mental health care through Lyra Empower, the only fully integrated, AI-powered platform combining the highest-quality care and technology solutions. </div>","openingPlain":"About Lyra Health\nLyra Health is a leading provider of evidence-based mental health care, serving more than 20 million people globally in partnership with employers and more than 100 million through health plan and partner relationships. The company has delivered more than 15 million sessions of mental health care, published more than 35 peer-reviewed studies, and delivered unmatched outcomes in terms of access, clinical effectiveness, and cost efficiency. Extensive peer-reviewed research confirms Lyra’s transformative care model helps people recover twice as fast and results in a 26% annual reduction in overall healthcare claims costs. Lyra is transforming access to life-changing mental health care through Lyra Empower, the only fully integrated, AI-powered platform combining the highest-quality care and technology solutions. \n","descriptionBody":"<div>\n<p><strong>About The Role</strong></p>\n<p>We are seeking an experienced <strong>Director of Operations &ndash; Provider Performance</strong> to establish and execute a holistic provider performance strategy across all of Lyra&rsquo;s clinical service lines. In this role, you will lead a high-impact team operating at the intersection of clinical strategy, data analytics, and operational execution. Your mandate is to optimize provider performance which will further drive clinical quality, client access to care, and business results.</p>\n<p>As a strategic player-coach, you will partner closely with Service Line leaders, Clinical Operations, and Data Analytics to build scalable data infrastructure, operational tools, and executive reporting. You will translate complex performance insights into actionable dashboards and operational systems that drive data visibility for providers, managers and executive leadership.</p>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"About The Role\nWe are seeking an experienced Director of Operations – Provider Performance to establish and execute a holistic provider performance strategy across all of Lyra’s clinical service lines. In this role, you will lead a high-impact team operating at the intersection of clinical strategy, data analytics, and operational execution. Your mandate is to optimize provider performance which will further drive clinical quality, client access to care, and business results.\nAs a strategic player-coach, you will partner closely with Service Line leaders, Clinical Operations, and Data Analytics to build scalable data infrastructure, operational tools, and executive reporting. You will translate complex performance insights into actionable dashboards and operational systems that drive data visibility for providers, managers and executive leadership.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/lyrahealth/1fc1bb17-b865-4fb3-ac0a-7053569d2d59","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/lyrahealth/1fc1bb17-b865-4fb3-ac0a-7053569d2d59/apply"}